WEBVTT

00:41.291 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

01:33.677 --> 01:35.178
What the…

01:35.262 --> 01:37.180
There's nothing in the bag.

01:42.060 --> 01:45.772
You've been digging up this whole mountain
for three months straight.

01:45.856 --> 01:48.066
Who… are you?

01:48.150 --> 01:49.151
Where is Hanyang?

01:49.901 --> 01:52.154
- What?
- I need to get to Hanyang today.

01:52.237 --> 01:55.073
So, tell me. Which way is it?

01:57.159 --> 02:00.329
Hanyang is that way.

02:01.204 --> 02:03.081
Oh, that way?

02:03.874 --> 02:06.585
But it'll take at least 20 days
to get there.

02:11.381 --> 02:12.382
What?

02:20.432 --> 02:21.892
Oh, I almost forgot.

02:24.519 --> 02:27.105
Dig that up
and brew it carefully for half a day.

02:27.189 --> 02:29.066
It will help with your mother's illness.

02:29.816 --> 02:30.692
What?

02:44.581 --> 02:46.291
This is an ancient tale.

02:47.542 --> 02:49.878
I found it!

02:50.379 --> 02:52.089
It is the story of a nine-tailed fox

02:52.172 --> 02:53.674
who wished to become human,

02:53.757 --> 02:57.386
spending her days cultivating virtue
on Myohyangsan Mountain.

03:22.953 --> 03:25.122
Can you leave us for a moment?

03:25.956 --> 03:27.416
Chun-sim stays.

03:32.587 --> 03:34.005
Chun-sim.

03:34.631 --> 03:35.882
That's you!

03:46.727 --> 03:48.228
What did you do with Chun-sim?

03:49.938 --> 03:51.064
Pardon?

03:52.107 --> 03:53.066
What do you…

03:53.984 --> 03:55.110
Look.

03:57.779 --> 03:59.239
It's so obvious.

04:05.328 --> 04:08.623
You seemed completely human,
yet your cunning is all fox.

04:08.707 --> 04:09.583
How did you know?

04:10.542 --> 04:11.668
Your scent.

04:11.752 --> 04:13.837
I smell the earth on you.

04:13.920 --> 04:17.132
The scent of Myohyangsan Mountain's soil
that I've known for centuries.

04:18.383 --> 04:19.342
Have you been well?

04:20.761 --> 04:25.474
I was just bored without you around.

04:26.641 --> 04:28.727
By the way, don't worry about Chun-sim.

04:29.227 --> 04:31.188
I bet she's dozing off in the kitchen.

04:31.730 --> 04:32.606
All right.

04:34.566 --> 04:35.484
How do you feel?

04:36.151 --> 04:37.736
It's your long-awaited wedding day.

04:39.488 --> 04:41.198
It still doesn't feel real

04:41.907 --> 04:45.285
that I've become human
and will be wed to my beloved.

04:46.578 --> 04:47.496
Goodness.

04:48.121 --> 04:51.625
Fine, leave me behind
and go live a happy life.

04:53.752 --> 04:56.338
Come here, Eun-ho.
Let me hug you. It's been a while.

04:57.798 --> 04:59.299
Geum-ho…

05:29.454 --> 05:31.706
This is usually where old tales end.

05:34.376 --> 05:38.046
She finally became human
and married the one she loved.

05:39.214 --> 05:42.759
And so, they lived happily ever after.

05:43.885 --> 05:44.928
The end.

05:47.806 --> 05:49.015
Get over here!

05:51.768 --> 05:53.019
Wow, amazing.

05:55.188 --> 05:56.439
Look at this.

05:56.523 --> 05:58.567
These hairpins must be new.

05:58.650 --> 06:00.861
Oh my gosh, they're so pretty!

06:01.862 --> 06:02.988
Don't they look good on me?

06:06.992 --> 06:08.994
- Geum-ho?
- Yes?

06:12.205 --> 06:14.416
What's got you staring like that?

06:23.258 --> 06:25.176
Well, look at you.

06:26.595 --> 06:28.263
What?

06:29.598 --> 06:31.975
So that's why
you wanted to come to the market.

06:32.058 --> 06:33.852
You had an ulterior motive.

06:35.270 --> 06:36.396
It's not like that.

06:36.479 --> 06:37.898
If you're done looking, let's go.

06:39.316 --> 06:40.442
My lady!

06:45.906 --> 06:47.824
So we meet again.

06:49.326 --> 06:50.827
Yes, my lord.

06:51.453 --> 06:53.830
What a coincidence running into you.

07:04.966 --> 07:06.843
Be happy, Geum-ho.

07:23.568 --> 07:25.779
But I didn't know then…

07:28.073 --> 07:29.282
That way!

07:29.908 --> 07:32.953
…that human life is endlessly fragile,

07:33.036 --> 07:36.039
and their happiness
shatters far too easily.

07:38.500 --> 07:42.545
That life is hard,
and death is always near.

07:44.130 --> 07:46.883
That was the future that awaited.

07:48.843 --> 07:52.973
So in the end,
Geum-ho would not find happiness.

07:54.182 --> 07:57.602
All because she loved a human
and chose to become one.

07:59.771 --> 08:03.400
PRESENT DAY

08:04.943 --> 08:07.529
And so, I became who I am today.

08:08.738 --> 08:10.615
A nine-tailed fox
who refuses to love humans

08:10.699 --> 08:12.450
and does not seek to become one.

08:13.076 --> 08:14.077
That's who I am.

08:20.375 --> 08:23.044
Why should I want to become a human?

08:23.128 --> 08:26.423
So trivial, powerless, aging, sickly,

08:26.506 --> 08:28.925
and in the end, doomed to die.

08:32.679 --> 08:34.139
Here and now,

08:35.640 --> 08:37.559
one life ends…

08:40.061 --> 08:42.022
and another begins.

08:45.525 --> 08:50.447
And this story began nine years ago.

08:56.786 --> 09:01.124
EPISODE 1
AN INEVITABLE EVENT

09:02.167 --> 09:03.626
Here! Over here!

09:03.710 --> 09:04.919
SOSIN HIGH SCHOOL

09:07.756 --> 09:09.049
HYEON WOO-SEOK

09:09.132 --> 09:10.258
Pass! Over there!

09:10.341 --> 09:11.885
Cover! I'm coming through!

09:11.968 --> 09:12.927
NINE YEARS AGO

09:13.011 --> 09:14.345
That's it!

09:15.305 --> 09:17.140
He's good, isn't he?

09:17.223 --> 09:19.017
That's Hyeon Woo-seok.

09:19.100 --> 09:20.935
He just became a high school senior.

09:25.732 --> 09:28.443
Since he was first selected
for the U-13 national team,

09:28.526 --> 09:31.237
he has been the starting striker
across all youth squads.

09:35.867 --> 09:37.786
Hey, Woo-seok! Pass!

09:39.537 --> 09:41.748
- Pass!
- Cover this side!

09:41.831 --> 09:44.042
Hey! You crazy idiot!

09:44.125 --> 09:45.418
Woo-seok was open!

09:45.502 --> 09:47.921
Stop messing around
and just pass the ball!

09:49.130 --> 09:51.341
He's asking who that player is.

09:51.424 --> 09:52.759
Which one?

09:55.303 --> 09:56.387
- That one.
- Hey!

09:56.471 --> 09:58.515
- Hey, that's a foul!
- The one messing around earlier.

09:58.598 --> 10:00.225
That's Kang Si-yeol.

10:00.308 --> 10:02.644
Gosh, that kid is just crazy.

10:02.727 --> 10:05.188
He's all flash and no substance.
And he never passes.

10:05.271 --> 10:07.315
He tries to do everything himself.

10:13.530 --> 10:16.491
Hey, Si-yeol, you brat! Just tap it in!

10:16.574 --> 10:18.201
Stop showing off!

10:24.958 --> 10:26.251
Damn, that little…

10:27.669 --> 10:30.380
Woo-seok, nice assist.

10:30.463 --> 10:32.132
Assist.

10:34.134 --> 10:38.012
You think what a coach says is a joke?

10:38.096 --> 10:41.474
I told you to pass to Woo-seok
whenever you get the ball.

10:41.558 --> 10:47.230
The new youth national team coach
came to watch Woo-seok play today.

10:47.313 --> 10:49.440
The least you could do
is help your friend,

10:50.108 --> 10:51.526
not get in his way.

10:54.362 --> 10:56.865
How is me scoring a goal
getting in Woo-seok's way?

10:57.949 --> 11:01.119
So why did you have to score a goal?

11:01.703 --> 11:04.080
I told you to play defense today.

11:04.164 --> 11:06.708
When did I tell you to score a goal?

11:07.625 --> 11:09.586
You got carried away trying to stand out.

11:09.669 --> 11:10.795
Straighten up.

11:15.592 --> 11:19.053
You've never even paid
your club fees on time,

11:19.637 --> 11:21.139
and you give me this attitude.

11:24.267 --> 11:25.268
Good work.

11:25.351 --> 11:26.853
- Hey, boys.
- Eat up.

11:26.936 --> 11:28.855
Woo-seok's father is treating us,

11:28.938 --> 11:30.899
so make sure you thank him
before digging in.

11:30.982 --> 11:32.859
Gosh, Coach. There's really no need.

11:35.570 --> 11:37.488
- Here, have some more.
- Hey, Kang Si-yeol.

11:37.572 --> 11:38.656
LET'S GO, SOSIN SOCCER CLUB!

11:38.740 --> 11:39.866
Dad, hold on.

11:39.949 --> 11:41.284
- Sure.
- Hold this.

11:42.327 --> 11:44.871
- Kang Si-yeol.
- It's fine. I don't want any.

11:50.084 --> 11:51.336
Coach.

11:51.419 --> 11:53.546
Yes, good to see you.

11:53.630 --> 11:55.590
- Great game today.
- Not at all.

11:55.673 --> 11:58.968
Here, use this to take the boys out
for a nice dinner next time.

11:59.052 --> 12:00.970
Thank you as always, Mr. Hyeon.

12:02.472 --> 12:04.265
- Thank you.
- It's nothing.

12:06.017 --> 12:08.269
The contractor for Bannam Zone 2,

12:08.353 --> 12:11.814
Korea's biggest redevelopment project,
will be named today.

12:11.898 --> 12:15.401
With three top-tier construction companies
competing for the contract,

12:15.485 --> 12:19.072
experts say Geumsu Construction,
embroiled in a power abuse scandal,

12:19.155 --> 12:22.867
is unlikely to win, leaving the other two
as front-runners.

12:22.951 --> 12:24.077
In other news--

12:25.745 --> 12:26.871
Why did you turn it off?

12:28.164 --> 12:29.707
I was listening to it.

12:30.208 --> 12:32.585
I'm sorry, Mr. Lee.
Should I turn it back on?

12:34.921 --> 12:39.342
The real issue isn't abuse of power.
It's subordinates getting out of line.

12:39.425 --> 12:42.762
I pay you to drive,
so why aren't you focused on driving?

12:43.471 --> 12:44.973
Mr. Lee, it's not that--

12:45.056 --> 12:46.474
Are your ears perking up

12:47.433 --> 12:50.228
because they're trashing me on the radio?

12:50.311 --> 12:51.562
No, sir.

12:51.646 --> 12:53.439
That's not it at all.

12:53.523 --> 12:54.399
It's a red light.

12:56.025 --> 12:56.943
What the heck?

13:00.154 --> 13:02.073
Watch where you're going!

13:04.075 --> 13:05.660
2016 SEOUL
BANNAM ZONE 2 PROJECT PLAN

13:08.121 --> 13:10.456
It fell. What bad luck.

13:25.513 --> 13:29.392
WELCOME TO THE CONTRACTOR SELECTION
GENERAL MEETING

13:29.475 --> 13:31.144
Did you drive here yourself?

13:31.936 --> 13:33.271
I ended up driving myself.

13:33.980 --> 13:36.733
Mr. Lee, there's also
the board's decision to consider.

13:36.816 --> 13:37.984
Are you sure about this?

13:38.067 --> 13:41.070
You mean those old geezers
telling me to stay put?

13:41.154 --> 13:43.781
There's no need
for you to get involved, sir.

13:43.865 --> 13:46.659
It was always going to be
a difficult contract to win.

13:46.743 --> 13:49.871
Now there's a risk that
you might have to take all the blame.

13:49.954 --> 13:52.290
This is why you're just an employee.

13:56.461 --> 13:58.379
- Just take off your shirt.
- Yes, sir.

13:58.463 --> 14:00.923
- Should I hire a new driver?
- Sure, whatever.

14:01.007 --> 14:03.718
Just give him some money
so he doesn't run his mouth.

14:03.801 --> 14:04.927
Yes, sir.

14:12.018 --> 14:13.853
This project is mine.

14:13.936 --> 14:17.148
I want every son of a bitch
in the sticks to know

14:17.231 --> 14:20.693
that Lee Yoon of Geumsu Group
personally won a 9.5-trillion-won project.

14:20.777 --> 14:24.155
Then those old geezers won't be able
to call me a deadbeat anymore.

14:25.656 --> 14:26.657
Mr. Lee.

14:27.325 --> 14:29.869
Now is a crucial time,
with the group's succession on the line.

14:29.952 --> 14:31.537
If you fail to win the contract--

14:31.621 --> 14:34.540
You know that saying,
"there's nothing money can't buy"?

14:34.624 --> 14:36.793
I used to think
that was just an expression.

14:37.335 --> 14:38.461
But I was wrong.

14:38.544 --> 14:41.339
There's nothing that money can't solve.

14:41.422 --> 14:44.300
Seriously, anything's possible with money.

14:51.432 --> 14:55.603
Dear fellow members
of the Bannam Zone 2 union,

14:56.229 --> 14:58.564
to begin, we,
the executive team of Yeoni Construction,

14:58.648 --> 15:01.776
would like to extend our deepest respects
to the union members.

15:02.693 --> 15:04.487
BANNAM ZONE 2 CONSTRUCTION PROJECT PLAN

15:07.573 --> 15:09.575
What, a deep bow? Give me a break.

15:12.787 --> 15:13.871
YEONI CONSTRUCTION

15:21.462 --> 15:22.588
I'm sorry, sir.

15:25.216 --> 15:26.843
Hey, what did you do?

15:26.926 --> 15:28.886
- Aren't they starting?
- What's going on?

15:30.847 --> 15:32.557
- Jeez.
- What are they doing?

15:33.933 --> 15:37.061
What's this?
Did they hire another celebrity?

15:37.145 --> 15:38.271
My dear humans.

15:38.354 --> 15:40.106
Allow me to intrude for a bit.

15:40.189 --> 15:41.357
What is going on right now?

15:41.441 --> 15:42.733
- What…
- Who's she?

15:42.817 --> 15:44.193
It's a little noisy.

15:44.819 --> 15:47.947
Don't panic.
Starting now, you will lose your voices.

15:50.992 --> 15:52.952
Now, everyone focus on me.

15:53.035 --> 15:54.162
Don't think of anything else.

16:11.721 --> 16:14.557
I'm sure you're all very busy,
so I'll make this quick.

16:15.224 --> 16:19.437
You must all be stressing over
who to vote for to make more money.

16:19.520 --> 16:22.482
But really, does it even matter
who builds the new Bannam-dong apartments?

16:22.565 --> 16:24.400
Don't overthink it.

16:25.943 --> 16:28.362
Everyone on the left side,
just vote for Geumsu Construction.

16:28.446 --> 16:30.865
As for everyone on the right,
do as you please.

16:31.616 --> 16:32.825
Well then.

16:35.620 --> 16:36.496
Oh, right.

16:36.579 --> 16:37.955
Honestly, I feel a little bad.

16:38.039 --> 16:41.876
I have a general idea of how much
you humans love your apartments.

16:42.543 --> 16:45.463
But what can I do?
I have to make money too.

16:45.546 --> 16:47.798
I'm sure you all understand
since we all love money.

16:47.882 --> 16:49.800
Right? Bye then.

16:58.518 --> 16:59.977
You. Follow me.

17:35.012 --> 17:36.556
Oh dear.

17:40.184 --> 17:41.310
Goodness.

17:41.394 --> 17:42.895
- Grandma, let me.
- What?

17:44.647 --> 17:47.024
All right, let's go.

17:51.404 --> 17:52.780
I scored a goal today.

17:53.364 --> 17:54.991
Oh my, well done.

17:56.701 --> 17:58.911
- Is that it?
- What else should I say?

17:58.995 --> 18:01.122
I'm just saying "well done"
because you did well.

18:01.205 --> 18:03.749
My goodness, Grandma.

18:03.833 --> 18:06.919
If you keep this up,
I won't spoil you when I'm older.

18:07.920 --> 18:11.299
I don't care about that.

18:11.382 --> 18:13.301
Well, I care.

18:13.384 --> 18:14.802
Just you wait.

18:15.428 --> 18:18.806
By the way, when do we need to pay
this month's soccer club fee?

18:20.308 --> 18:22.852
I told you not to worry about that.

18:24.478 --> 18:25.980
I'm exempt from the fees.

18:26.606 --> 18:27.773
I'm the star player, you know.

18:28.733 --> 18:31.611
Still, that's not how things should be.

18:31.694 --> 18:34.572
Grandma, haven't you heard
of a full scholarship?

18:35.197 --> 18:37.658
I don't have to pay a single penny.

18:38.326 --> 18:39.535
Gosh, really?

18:39.619 --> 18:42.079
Oh, my little boy, I'm so proud of you.

18:52.256 --> 18:54.175
- Enjoy your meal. Take care.
- Thank you.

18:55.259 --> 18:56.719
Here you go. Be safe!

19:01.140 --> 19:02.099
Enjoy your meal.

19:02.183 --> 19:03.517
SPEEDY DELIVERY SERVICE

19:11.275 --> 19:12.151
Thank you.

19:30.711 --> 19:32.797
What are you doing at this hour?

19:35.549 --> 19:38.010
What about you?
And what's with that outfit?

19:38.969 --> 19:41.138
I'm working my part-time job.

19:41.764 --> 19:43.724
- What?
- I've got my eye on some cleats.

19:44.767 --> 19:47.186
Jeez, you should be spending
your time practicing.

19:47.269 --> 19:49.230
Just ask your parents for the cleats.

19:58.072 --> 19:59.907
- Hey, wanna make a bet?
- Jeez.

20:03.786 --> 20:05.037
What are the stakes?

20:36.819 --> 20:39.071
- Hey, that was a clear foul!
- Goal!

20:39.155 --> 20:40.781
You're out.

20:47.997 --> 20:49.165
Goal!

20:49.790 --> 20:51.375
- Left.
- Right.

20:58.758 --> 20:59.967
It went in, right?

21:01.385 --> 21:03.053
Goal!

21:08.809 --> 21:09.894
Nice.

21:17.443 --> 21:21.280
I was wondering why you were playing
like your life depended on it.

21:21.363 --> 21:23.491
But is that it? A chicken breast?

21:23.574 --> 21:25.242
I wasn't playing like that.

21:25.326 --> 21:27.328
I just crushed you with my skills.

21:28.954 --> 21:31.332
What? Are you hurt?

21:31.415 --> 21:33.542
Hey, just hurry up and eat.

21:33.626 --> 21:35.795
I want to get a few more deliveries in.

21:39.048 --> 21:42.301
What, is this your thing?

21:42.384 --> 21:43.886
A lazy genius?

21:44.720 --> 21:48.057
I mean, you don't seem to be taking
private lessons like everyone else.

21:48.140 --> 21:49.809
And you're working part-time at this hour.

21:51.769 --> 21:53.854
But seeing you in action…

21:57.358 --> 21:58.818
You asshole!

22:00.152 --> 22:01.403
Hey.

22:02.196 --> 22:03.572
A poor genius.

22:04.281 --> 22:05.199
What?

22:05.282 --> 22:08.202
You got the genius part right,
but I'm a bit short on cash.

22:09.119 --> 22:10.830
My parents aren't around,

22:10.913 --> 22:12.331
and my grandma's sick.

22:14.041 --> 22:15.042
I see.

22:15.125 --> 22:18.003
So while you're practicing,
I have to be out making money.

22:18.629 --> 22:19.755
Hey, I didn't know--

22:19.839 --> 22:21.924
But you know what's really important here?

22:22.925 --> 22:26.887
Despite all that,
without any of those damn private lessons,

22:26.971 --> 22:29.515
I still managed to kick your ass today.

22:29.598 --> 22:32.142
You saw the goal I scored
during practice today, right?

22:32.977 --> 22:34.895
Yeah, I saw it, you punk.

22:35.938 --> 22:39.191
So don't get too cocky
just because you're on the national team.

22:39.275 --> 22:42.862
When you get called up,
I'm gonna take your spot as striker.

22:43.988 --> 22:47.575
When you get back, the starting lineup
might be totally different.

22:47.658 --> 22:49.493
Why am I even talking to you?

22:50.077 --> 22:50.995
Jeez.

22:52.746 --> 22:53.831
Man, that's good.

22:55.833 --> 22:57.293
You really don't want any?

22:57.376 --> 22:58.836
I don't eat stuff like that.

23:10.598 --> 23:12.057
Why aren't you eating?

23:13.183 --> 23:15.311
That poor cow died for nothing.

23:15.394 --> 23:16.770
I don't have an appetite.

23:16.854 --> 23:19.064
I told you,
there's nothing to worry about.

23:19.690 --> 23:21.275
This is important to me.

23:22.902 --> 23:25.362
I'm sure it is.

23:25.988 --> 23:27.323
You acted like a deadbeat,

23:27.406 --> 23:29.658
and now you're
on your rich father's bad side.

23:29.742 --> 23:31.994
And now your position as heir is at risk.

23:33.245 --> 23:35.456
You seem pretty interested
in human affairs.

23:35.956 --> 23:37.708
Because I've taken a liking to you.

23:38.417 --> 23:41.086
You're rich,
and you look like a troublemaker.

23:41.170 --> 23:43.464
I think you're going to become
a repeat customer.

23:43.547 --> 23:45.341
Since we're on the subject,

23:46.592 --> 23:48.594
who are your other clients besides me?

23:50.387 --> 23:53.223
You seem pretty interested
in nine-tailed fox affairs.

23:56.060 --> 23:57.770
Can I have this one too?

24:01.106 --> 24:03.025
I guess that's a secret.

24:06.070 --> 24:07.988
Then, what exactly are you capable of?

24:09.531 --> 24:11.951
Judging by the fact that you need money,

24:12.034 --> 24:14.453
it seems you can't do whatever you want.

24:14.536 --> 24:18.040
Shouldn't I know
what you can and can't do

24:19.249 --> 24:21.168
if I'm going to hire you again?

24:21.877 --> 24:23.796
Humans are always like this.

24:25.255 --> 24:27.883
All right, let me explain something.

24:39.937 --> 24:40.896
What is this?

24:42.731 --> 24:43.941
Where am I?

24:44.024 --> 24:47.277
I guess calling you a "customer"
gave you the wrong idea.

24:47.361 --> 24:49.989
That if you just give me money,
you can order me to do anything

24:50.072 --> 24:51.532
and ask for whatever you want.

25:02.376 --> 25:03.585
Simply put,

25:03.669 --> 25:06.213
think of this less as making requests
and more like praying.

25:07.172 --> 25:10.217
Whether or not I grant your wish
is up to me.

25:10.300 --> 25:12.970
And how I choose to grant it
is also up to me.

25:13.053 --> 25:15.389
How much I take,
and what I take as payment,

25:15.472 --> 25:17.516
is obviously up to me as well.

25:17.599 --> 25:20.310
I'm the one who asks questions, not you.

25:20.394 --> 25:24.273
Even what you're allowed to know,
and how much, is up to me.

25:26.567 --> 25:28.485
Do you understand now?

25:29.069 --> 25:31.488
I'm telling you not to get cocky.

25:32.114 --> 25:33.907
You pathetic little human.

25:38.495 --> 25:41.248
But since we're on the subject,
I'll tell you one thing.

25:41.331 --> 25:43.459
I have only one principle.

25:43.542 --> 25:45.753
I avoid doing
even the smallest of good deeds

25:45.836 --> 25:47.671
and only avoid doing major misdeeds.

25:50.966 --> 25:53.135
Looks like you didn't get it.

25:53.218 --> 25:55.971
This is important,
so I'll break it down for you.

25:56.055 --> 25:59.141
I don't do good deeds.
No matter how trivial.

25:59.767 --> 26:03.062
I can't risk cultivating more virtue
and accidentally becoming human.

26:03.145 --> 26:05.773
As for wrongdoings,
I only avoid major ones.

26:05.856 --> 26:07.858
Things like…

26:09.401 --> 26:10.611
killing people.

26:11.445 --> 26:12.821
That's the only thing I avoid.

26:12.905 --> 26:16.617
I'm trying to avoid becoming human,
not trying to diminish my spiritual power.

26:19.578 --> 26:20.454
SECRETARY CHOI

26:25.250 --> 26:26.210
You can go now.

26:27.795 --> 26:31.048
The voting results are out.
You should go get your picture taken.

26:31.131 --> 26:33.133
Nothing beats a photo for showing off.

26:33.842 --> 26:37.179
By the way, I already took the money
from the trunk of your car.

26:37.262 --> 26:38.430
So don't worry about it.

27:20.597 --> 27:24.601
A human's life
is like swimming in a sea of suffering.

27:26.562 --> 27:29.648
From the moment they're thrown
into this unfamiliar world

27:29.731 --> 27:32.317
until they rot away to nothing,

27:32.401 --> 27:35.529
humans can never find
even a moment of peace.

27:38.407 --> 27:40.868
Life is a constant competition.

27:43.745 --> 27:44.788
It's a battlefield

27:44.872 --> 27:47.499
where they can only climb up
by dragging others down.

27:50.919 --> 27:53.797
And it's a hamster wheel
that never stops turning.

27:57.384 --> 28:00.888
Human happiness
is but a fleeting illusion,

28:00.971 --> 28:05.058
and such is the human condition
I have observed for hundreds of years.

28:07.352 --> 28:10.606
But in contrast to that,
my life as a nine-tailed fox

28:10.689 --> 28:13.066
is like a festival that never ends.

28:27.789 --> 28:28.790
Hey.

28:30.876 --> 28:32.127
Yes?

28:32.211 --> 28:34.630
All the kids these days
seem to dress like you.

28:34.713 --> 28:37.174
I used to dress like that 20 years ago.

28:37.257 --> 28:40.010
- I guess it's back in style.
- Excuse me?

28:40.093 --> 28:41.011
You.

28:41.094 --> 28:43.347
Come shopping with me today.

28:44.097 --> 28:44.973
Why should I?

28:45.057 --> 28:47.226
Because I like the way you dress.

28:47.851 --> 28:50.103
Besides, it's boring to shop alone.

28:50.646 --> 28:53.774
Think of yourself
as a friend for the day, if you will.

28:54.358 --> 28:56.026
What the heck?

28:56.109 --> 28:57.778
What a weirdo.

29:00.280 --> 29:01.240
Listen to me.

29:01.323 --> 29:04.034
You're going to hang out with me today.

29:06.078 --> 29:07.037
Yes, of course.

29:08.747 --> 29:11.833
So, you're saying
you're a nine-tailed fox?

29:11.917 --> 29:13.293
Really?

29:13.377 --> 29:15.796
Come on, a nine-tailed fox?

29:15.879 --> 29:18.048
There's no such thing.

29:18.131 --> 29:20.467
You'd believe me if I used sorcery
and showed you my tails,

29:20.550 --> 29:22.219
but I can't be bothered.

29:23.971 --> 29:26.473
Just believe it. I'm a nine-tailed fox.

29:27.516 --> 29:29.559
Oh, okay.

29:31.436 --> 29:34.273
Oh my! Those look great on you too.

29:34.356 --> 29:35.649
You think so?

29:35.732 --> 29:36.775
I'll take these too.

29:39.027 --> 29:41.697
Hey, I have a question.

29:41.780 --> 29:42.781
What is it?

29:42.864 --> 29:46.159
"Aren't nine-tailed foxes
supposed to eat human livers

29:46.243 --> 29:49.246
and seduce men to drain their life force?"

29:49.329 --> 29:51.123
Yes, how did you know?

29:52.124 --> 29:53.583
It was obvious.

29:53.667 --> 29:57.004
Do you think you're the first human
to ask me such questions?

29:57.713 --> 30:00.340
Do you know how people
in the Joseon era used to speak?

30:01.883 --> 30:02.843
You think they were like…

30:02.926 --> 30:04.803
"Your Majesty."

30:04.886 --> 30:06.013
"How insolent!"

30:06.888 --> 30:08.515
Do you really think that?

30:08.598 --> 30:09.516
They didn't?

30:09.599 --> 30:12.477
That's all just made up
by those TV people.

30:13.603 --> 30:16.064
It's not as if they actually
lived through that era like I did.

30:16.148 --> 30:18.275
So how would they know?

30:18.358 --> 30:22.070
You make something up,
and humans just believe it.

30:23.405 --> 30:25.073
Same with the tales
about nine-tailed foxes.

30:25.157 --> 30:27.117
My goodness, that's truly amazing.

30:27.200 --> 30:30.829
Look at everything happening
inside that little box.

30:30.912 --> 30:32.581
My goodness, how fascinating!

30:33.540 --> 30:34.916
RETURN OF THE LEGEND
NINE-TAILED FOX

30:35.000 --> 30:37.169
People didn't think of us in this way

30:37.252 --> 30:39.379
before that damn Return of the Legend.

30:51.516 --> 30:54.102
Oh my gosh.
That scared the life out of me.

30:57.147 --> 30:59.691
When humans cultivate themselves,
they're called sages,

30:59.775 --> 31:01.902
while animals that do so
are called spirit beasts.

31:01.985 --> 31:05.280
So why do foxes cultivating themselves
to become human get treated like monsters?

31:05.364 --> 31:09.326
Do they think it's easy to self-cultivate
and train until we grow nine tails?

31:09.409 --> 31:11.370
Nine-tailed foxes cultivate themselves?

31:11.453 --> 31:14.956
Yes, just like how sages self-cultivate
and train to become immortals,

31:15.040 --> 31:17.793
nine-tailed foxes have to self-cultivate
and train to become humans.

31:17.876 --> 31:18.752
Think about it.

31:18.835 --> 31:21.546
Why would a nine-tailed fox,
who's self-cultivating and building karma,

31:21.630 --> 31:23.048
hunt human livers? If they did that,

31:23.131 --> 31:25.801
they would lose
all the spiritual power they've earned.

31:26.510 --> 31:28.637
Oh, I see.

31:29.763 --> 31:31.598
You must have felt so misunderstood.

31:32.349 --> 31:34.226
Anyway, that's all in the past.

31:34.309 --> 31:36.853
I'm the only nine-tailed fox
left on Earth now.

31:36.937 --> 31:40.816
I've lost all desire to be human,
so I have no reason to cultivate myself.

31:40.899 --> 31:42.692
You're not trying to become human?

31:42.776 --> 31:44.611
But you're a nine-tailed fox. How come?

31:44.694 --> 31:46.738
Because I love the way I live now.

31:47.489 --> 31:49.783
Sometimes, humans get the wrong idea.

31:49.866 --> 31:53.120
They think that living forever
would be tedious and boring.

31:53.203 --> 31:56.331
But when you actually experience it,
there's never a dull moment

31:56.415 --> 31:58.500
because the human world changes so fast.

31:59.376 --> 32:02.796
There's always something new and fun.

32:04.297 --> 32:08.385
Shoeshine! Shoeshine!

32:08.468 --> 32:11.930
YEAR 1930

32:13.557 --> 32:14.474
Shoeshine!

32:14.558 --> 32:15.725
- It's English.
- At our academy…

32:15.809 --> 32:18.270
YEJEONG ACADEMY

32:18.353 --> 32:20.897
ENGLISH
YOUR WEAPON FOR SUCCESS!

32:24.025 --> 32:26.778
So this is how Westerners write?

32:27.988 --> 32:29.281
This looks like it'd be fun.

32:49.342 --> 32:51.344
What did that Westerner just say?

32:54.264 --> 32:55.682
Hey, Teacher.

32:55.765 --> 32:58.643
Speak our language.
I can't understand a single word.

33:01.605 --> 33:02.981
What did you just say?

33:03.064 --> 33:07.736
How am I suddenly speaking
in Joseon language?

33:07.819 --> 33:09.362
Oh, Lord!

33:10.363 --> 33:11.656
YEAR 1970

33:11.781 --> 33:12.908
COMICS
MARTIAL ARTS, ROMANCE

33:12.991 --> 33:15.494
THE COUNT'S BLACK SHEEP
FINAL EPISODE

33:22.125 --> 33:23.585
THE END

33:23.668 --> 33:24.628
What?

33:25.462 --> 33:27.547
The main character dies?

33:30.926 --> 33:33.136
What kind of ending is this?

33:33.220 --> 33:34.554
Hey, you. Comic artist.

33:35.138 --> 33:36.181
Hey, comic artist!

33:39.893 --> 33:41.353
Who are you?

33:43.313 --> 33:44.523
What's with this ending?

33:44.606 --> 33:46.775
Is this the best you could do?

33:47.317 --> 33:48.527
Draw it again!

33:51.321 --> 33:52.864
THE COUNT'S BLACK SHEEP
FINAL EPISODE

33:59.037 --> 34:00.330
What's happening?

34:05.168 --> 34:06.836
THE END

34:10.006 --> 34:11.967
SPACE ARCADE
MAKKEULLAE RICKSHAW

34:12.050 --> 34:13.885
YEAR 1990

34:14.010 --> 34:16.221
THE 4TH NATIONAL GAMING TOURNAMENT
PRELIMINARY ROUND

34:24.145 --> 34:27.649
Hey, stop it! Stop following me!

34:31.319 --> 34:33.488
You're such a cheap player.

34:34.739 --> 34:36.575
Stop beating me.

34:37.242 --> 34:38.660
Please, just stop.

34:57.470 --> 35:00.432
Hey, don't make it so obvious!
It's no fun now.

35:00.515 --> 35:02.517
Do your best, okay?

35:03.143 --> 35:05.186
Play better, but not to win.

35:05.812 --> 35:07.188
Is that so hard?

35:07.272 --> 35:08.523
But, seriously,

35:09.024 --> 35:11.109
is it really fun to live like that?

35:11.985 --> 35:12.861
What?

35:12.944 --> 35:16.114
I mean, what you're saying is
that in all that time,

35:16.197 --> 35:18.366
you've never actually
accomplished anything.

35:19.326 --> 35:20.869
What is that supposed to mean?

35:20.952 --> 35:22.621
You don't think
I've accomplished anything?

35:22.704 --> 35:25.248
I've learned everything
and played every game there is.

35:25.332 --> 35:29.252
But no matter what you've learned,
you haven't followed through.

35:29.336 --> 35:32.130
If there's something you don't like,
you just change it all.

35:32.213 --> 35:34.549
- Or just scrap it.
- It's not like that.

35:34.633 --> 35:36.968
And you don't have any friends
to shop and chat with,

35:37.052 --> 35:38.553
so you just grab a random person and--

35:38.637 --> 35:39.846
I said it's not like that!

35:41.473 --> 35:42.849
Hey, take my side.

35:42.932 --> 35:44.017
No matter what.

35:46.603 --> 35:48.647
I envy you.

35:48.730 --> 35:50.398
I wish I could live like you.

35:50.482 --> 35:54.778
Just spending money and having fun
without a care in the world.

35:56.029 --> 35:57.322
What?

35:57.906 --> 35:59.199
Yes? What is it?

36:00.283 --> 36:02.952
Forget it. Just finish your food.

36:03.662 --> 36:05.330
I really chose the wrong person for this.

36:06.247 --> 36:09.334
Can't she read the room at all?

36:28.061 --> 36:29.688
What is it?

36:29.771 --> 36:32.023
Why did you drag me out on a weekend?

36:32.899 --> 36:34.526
Pick one. Whichever.

36:35.402 --> 36:36.319
What?

36:37.612 --> 36:40.031
You said there were cleats
you wanted to buy.

36:40.115 --> 36:42.992
Don't save up with your part-time job.
Just pick them now.

36:45.328 --> 36:47.539
And if I do?
You're going to buy them for me?

36:47.622 --> 36:49.249
No.

36:50.291 --> 36:52.919
I happen to have
a sponsorship deal with this brand.

36:53.002 --> 36:55.046
It's a sponsorship
worth 20 million won a year,

36:55.130 --> 36:57.549
but I can't use all of it
by myself anyway.

36:58.299 --> 36:59.426
A sponsorship deal?

37:00.093 --> 37:01.594
But you're not even a pro.

37:02.762 --> 37:06.433
Dude, I'm a top prospect
for the youth national team.

37:07.642 --> 37:10.019
They signed me a few years ago.

37:12.814 --> 37:14.816
Are you going to pick one or not?

37:14.899 --> 37:16.067
Do you think I'm a beggar?

37:17.736 --> 37:18.820
What?

37:19.487 --> 37:20.613
I'm fine.

37:22.657 --> 37:23.742
I'm leaving.

37:25.910 --> 37:26.953
Hey…

37:27.579 --> 37:30.874
SONGWONGAK CHINESE RESTAURANT

37:31.040 --> 37:33.376
That was so delicious.

37:33.460 --> 37:34.419
Yeah, I guess you--

37:39.132 --> 37:42.635
Humans are so pathetically weak.

37:48.600 --> 37:50.393
Get up. Is anything broken?

37:51.352 --> 37:52.520
No…

37:55.064 --> 37:56.733
No, that's not it.

37:58.985 --> 38:00.236
What happened?

38:00.320 --> 38:02.864
But are you okay?

38:02.947 --> 38:05.158
We ran into each other pretty hard.

38:05.241 --> 38:08.453
You should try exercising
instead of just burying yourself in books.

38:08.536 --> 38:09.954
You're pathetic for a guy your size.

38:10.038 --> 38:11.080
Just go.

38:16.753 --> 38:18.129
My apologies.

38:45.740 --> 38:46.950
How interesting.

38:47.575 --> 38:48.493
What is?

38:49.118 --> 38:50.453
That human over there.

38:50.537 --> 38:53.665
I think he'll become quite famous
in the near future.

38:54.541 --> 38:56.084
Famous?

38:56.584 --> 38:57.544
Which one of the two?

38:57.627 --> 38:58.920
That one over there.

39:02.590 --> 39:03.758
I see.

39:03.842 --> 39:06.761
But how do you know things like that?

39:06.845 --> 39:08.137
I just do.

39:08.763 --> 39:11.391
I sometimes see fragments of the future.

39:12.016 --> 39:13.726
I can't see them whenever I want.

39:13.810 --> 39:18.398
I don't know when, why, or what I'll see,

39:19.357 --> 39:22.193
but whatever I see is inevitable.

39:31.244 --> 39:32.579
That way!

39:36.291 --> 39:39.794
Even I can't do anything to change it.

39:43.172 --> 39:46.509
Anyway, that guy will become rich
and famous at some point.

39:47.135 --> 39:48.720
So he might become one of my clients.

39:48.803 --> 39:49.929
Oh, right.

39:50.013 --> 39:54.684
You said you grant rich people's wishes
and get paid for it, didn't you?

39:55.310 --> 39:57.312
Then, maybe you could grant my wish too?

39:58.813 --> 39:59.939
You think I would do that?

40:00.023 --> 40:03.318
You don't have nearly enough
to become my client.

40:03.401 --> 40:06.279
But starting today, we're friends.

40:06.362 --> 40:09.115
Don't you have, like,
a discount for friends and family?

40:10.116 --> 40:11.743
Humans never fail to disappoint.

40:12.911 --> 40:16.289
This is exactly why I don't bother
with troublesome human relationships.

40:16.372 --> 40:17.373
I told you earlier.

40:17.457 --> 40:19.542
You're just a friend for the day.

40:19.626 --> 40:20.501
What?

40:20.585 --> 40:22.378
What that means is…

40:24.505 --> 40:25.465
you're going to forget

40:25.548 --> 40:28.009
everything you did with me today,
everything we talked about,

40:28.092 --> 40:31.721
and even my very existence.

40:31.804 --> 40:33.097
Understand?

40:33.181 --> 40:34.432
Yes, I understand.

40:34.515 --> 40:36.601
Anyway, I had fun today.

40:36.684 --> 40:37.936
You should get going too.

40:49.364 --> 40:50.365
Hey, you guys.

40:52.492 --> 40:53.785
Come carry this for me.

41:12.887 --> 41:15.181
You're a beast cultivating yourself.

41:15.264 --> 41:17.433
What in the world are you doing here?

41:35.743 --> 41:36.744
Hey.

41:38.663 --> 41:39.789
Are you really mad?

41:42.750 --> 41:45.962
Look, it wasn't because
I felt sorry for you.

41:48.381 --> 41:49.340
Hey, come on.

41:53.011 --> 41:54.012
I'm sorry.

41:55.221 --> 41:59.851
I guess now that I think about it,
I did feel sorry for you.

42:01.144 --> 42:04.564
But it's not because I think
I'm better than you or anything.

42:04.647 --> 42:08.735
I just wanted to help you out
after what you told me.

42:10.695 --> 42:11.654
Hey.

42:12.280 --> 42:14.657
- What?
- Wanna kick the ball around a bit?

42:14.741 --> 42:16.117
What?

42:17.201 --> 42:18.703
ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

42:21.039 --> 42:22.623
Sure, bring it on.

42:32.050 --> 42:34.469
At cafés, you have to buy
one drink per person.

42:34.552 --> 42:36.804
That's the rule
in the human world these days.

42:37.346 --> 42:38.806
I'm…

42:40.391 --> 42:44.812
a being far greater
than any rule made by humans.

42:44.896 --> 42:46.314
I'm sure you are.

42:46.397 --> 42:48.816
After all,
you're the Deity of the Big Dipper.

42:50.818 --> 42:54.739
What brings you here all of a sudden,
interrupting my hobby like this?

42:54.822 --> 42:58.034
You call that a hobby?

42:58.117 --> 43:02.080
Of course. There isn't anything
more human and fun than spending money.

43:06.584 --> 43:09.087
If you enjoy living like a human so much,

43:09.170 --> 43:13.299
why won't you become one,
while deceiving the eyes of Heaven?

43:14.300 --> 43:16.552
You're missing the point.

43:16.636 --> 43:18.554
Who said I want to live like a human?

43:18.638 --> 43:20.640
Squeezing into the subway to go to work

43:20.723 --> 43:22.725
and working for over ten hours a day,

43:23.351 --> 43:25.353
only to collapse into sleep
from exhaustion.

43:25.436 --> 43:29.690
Even if you make a few bucks like that,
you don't have time to spend it.

43:30.316 --> 43:32.735
That's what it means to be human.

43:32.819 --> 43:36.155
A moment of sweetness,
and a lifetime of bitterness.

43:38.324 --> 43:42.829
But life as a nine-tailed fox is kind of
like spending money on a pay-to-win game.

43:42.912 --> 43:46.332
You get to enjoy all the fun stuff
without any of the inconvenience.

43:47.583 --> 43:51.379
I wonder if the big shots up there
would even understand what I'm saying.

43:51.462 --> 43:53.339
Since they're just so divine and all.

43:54.132 --> 43:55.925
You're still wicked and irreverent.

43:56.551 --> 43:58.678
Oh, whatever.

43:58.761 --> 44:01.264
Anyway, I don't think we're
on good enough terms to sit and chat.

44:01.347 --> 44:04.851
Let's just get straight to the point,
Lord Pagun.

44:04.934 --> 44:05.977
So?

44:07.228 --> 44:08.646
You want me to become human already?

44:08.729 --> 44:11.190
Are you asking why I'm still like this

44:11.274 --> 44:13.693
when all the other nine-tailed foxes
have already become human,

44:13.776 --> 44:16.195
lived out their lives, and died?

44:19.365 --> 44:20.658
I refuse.

44:20.741 --> 44:23.119
If that's all, I can go now, right?

44:23.202 --> 44:25.830
I'm going to go home
and unbox my new stuff.

44:25.913 --> 44:27.373
Your scale

44:28.040 --> 44:29.542
is tipping.

44:38.009 --> 44:38.926
That can't be.

44:40.136 --> 44:43.306
I put an insane amount of effort
into keeping that balance aligned.

44:43.973 --> 44:47.768
I even earn my own money
just to appease all of you up there.

44:48.311 --> 44:49.854
So how could the scale be tipping?

44:49.937 --> 44:52.982
There will come a time
when you must choose.

44:53.649 --> 44:55.651
Whether to become human

44:56.277 --> 44:59.739
or be forever annihilated.

45:04.327 --> 45:05.828
Don't make me laugh.

45:05.912 --> 45:09.248
They may be deities,
but how dare they threaten me?

45:12.126 --> 45:13.628
Let them try.

45:14.629 --> 45:18.633
Do they still think I'm the same
naive fox who believed everything

45:18.716 --> 45:20.635
the ones above told me?

45:21.177 --> 45:22.720
They won't get their way.

45:22.803 --> 45:26.432
Even you guys don't really get
the so-called Law of Heaven, do you?

45:26.515 --> 45:29.310
Because it's so vague and messed up.

45:29.393 --> 45:32.355
Well, there's one thing
I know for certain.

45:32.438 --> 45:35.483
"Heaven's net is vast and wide,
yet nothing slips through."

45:36.776 --> 45:39.695
You may think
you're outside of Heaven's influence,

45:39.779 --> 45:41.781
but nothing ever escapes notice.

45:44.367 --> 45:45.368
Ha!

45:45.868 --> 45:47.745
Save the sermon.

45:55.836 --> 45:57.880
That was Daoist teaching, actually.

46:02.551 --> 46:03.427
Excuse me.

46:05.221 --> 46:06.847
- Get up!
- Get up!

46:06.931 --> 46:08.182
Mr. Lee!

46:08.266 --> 46:10.101
- We love you!
- We love you!

46:10.184 --> 46:12.061
You're the only boss we have, sir!

46:14.272 --> 46:17.525
- Lee Yoon!
- Lee Yoon!

46:17.608 --> 46:19.568
What was that? I can't hear you.

46:19.652 --> 46:20.736
Louder!

46:20.820 --> 46:26.575
- Lee Yoon!
- Lee Yoon!

46:26.659 --> 46:28.327
Everyone, drink up!

46:28.411 --> 46:30.204
- Drink up!
- Drink up!

46:56.355 --> 46:57.565
Hey, are you okay?

46:59.191 --> 47:00.818
Gosh, let's call it a day.

47:00.901 --> 47:02.611
Hey, it's my turn though.

47:05.072 --> 47:06.198
Damn it.

47:08.034 --> 47:09.035
Fine.

47:15.916 --> 47:17.752
Unbelievable.

47:17.835 --> 47:20.463
I can't believe they're still
trying to boss me around at my age.

47:20.546 --> 47:21.839
Today just keeps getting worse--

47:24.050 --> 47:25.593
What? Who was that?

47:33.642 --> 47:35.770
Wow, it was like a missile.

47:35.853 --> 47:39.273
Hey, I'll go find the ball.
You go on ahead.

47:39.357 --> 47:41.859
- I'll come with you.
- It's fine. You go.

47:42.443 --> 47:43.569
Bye.

47:51.035 --> 47:52.661
Man, where did it go?

47:55.289 --> 47:56.624
Was it you?

47:59.377 --> 48:01.253
Are you the owner of this ball?

48:01.337 --> 48:02.421
Yes, I am.

48:02.505 --> 48:03.923
Thank you.

48:07.051 --> 48:09.095
- Wait.
- No need to thank me.

48:14.725 --> 48:17.603
- Hey--
- Go. We're done here.

48:17.686 --> 48:18.938
Excuse me!

48:22.525 --> 48:24.902
Wait, you're that kid from earlier.

48:24.985 --> 48:28.114
Were you kicking a ball around this late
because I told you to get some exercise?

48:28.197 --> 48:30.783
You don't look it,
but you're quite obedient.

48:30.866 --> 48:32.284
What is she talking about?

48:32.368 --> 48:35.287
You can't just pop
someone else's soccer ball like that.

48:35.371 --> 48:37.456
Well, I couldn't pop your head, could I?

48:37.540 --> 48:39.166
Since I'm a self-cultivated beast.

48:39.250 --> 48:40.793
Unbelievable.

48:43.504 --> 48:44.547
Hold on.

48:44.630 --> 48:46.382
They don't usually pop that easily.

48:46.465 --> 48:48.008
It's not some kind of balloon--

48:48.092 --> 48:50.719
That's because you are a weak human.

48:50.803 --> 48:52.179
What did you say?

48:52.263 --> 48:54.765
Wait, who do you keep calling weak?

48:55.307 --> 48:56.934
Can't you tell just by looking?

48:57.017 --> 48:57.935
I'm an athlete.

48:58.936 --> 49:00.020
Is that so?

49:00.104 --> 49:01.439
I may not be much right now,

49:01.522 --> 49:04.608
but in a few years,
I'm going to be a really famous athlete.

49:04.692 --> 49:05.943
Right.

49:07.194 --> 49:08.571
I don't think so.

49:09.071 --> 49:10.948
- What?
- Famous?

49:11.740 --> 49:13.033
Which one of the two?

49:13.617 --> 49:14.952
That one over there.

49:16.412 --> 49:18.289
Maybe your friend, but not you.

49:18.372 --> 49:19.540
I saw it earlier.

49:20.082 --> 49:21.250
What are you--

49:21.333 --> 49:23.669
Your friend is going to be very famous.

49:23.752 --> 49:26.338
He'll be a world-class player
and make a lot of money too.

49:26.422 --> 49:30.301
I'm certain. The future
never changes after I've seen it.

49:30.384 --> 49:32.094
But as for you…

49:37.850 --> 49:39.018
I don't see anything at all.

49:39.977 --> 49:42.354
Who are you to say that?

49:42.438 --> 49:44.190
You don't know anything about me!

49:44.732 --> 49:47.359
You'll just be a nobody.

49:47.443 --> 49:51.697
You might become a mediocre player
no one remembers,

49:51.780 --> 49:53.365
but any success beyond that…

49:55.075 --> 49:56.911
It's just not in your future.

49:57.620 --> 50:00.372
So don't get your hopes up
and dream too big.

50:00.456 --> 50:02.166
That way, you won't get hurt.

50:02.249 --> 50:03.459
This…

50:03.542 --> 50:05.628
This woman is a complete lunatic.

50:05.711 --> 50:06.837
It's cruel, I know.

50:08.547 --> 50:11.217
But that's just how human life is.

50:11.300 --> 50:13.636
It's not like life is being
especially cruel to you.

50:13.719 --> 50:15.054
So don't take it too hard.

50:19.850 --> 50:23.437
Man, I did it! Damn it!

50:24.146 --> 50:27.149
I'm Lee Yoon. Who's going to stop me?

50:30.945 --> 50:32.863
Move! Damn it!

50:54.885 --> 50:57.179
- Did you hear that?
- I don't know.

50:57.263 --> 50:58.681
Maybe there was an accident.

50:59.473 --> 51:01.183
It has nothing to do with me.

51:10.401 --> 51:13.112
Oh no, oh no… What…

51:18.951 --> 51:21.287
I have to get out of here.

51:25.749 --> 51:28.252
Hey!

51:28.335 --> 51:30.629
Stop! I said stop!

51:31.547 --> 51:32.798
Damn it.

51:33.382 --> 51:35.217
I said stop!

51:42.391 --> 51:43.475
Woo-seok!

51:44.184 --> 51:45.394
Woo-seok!

51:47.479 --> 51:49.023
Woo-seok.

51:59.283 --> 52:00.451
OPERATING ROOM

52:03.245 --> 52:04.663
You can't come in.

52:14.256 --> 52:15.924
PLEASE DISPOSE OF TRASH HERE

52:16.008 --> 52:17.176
Damn it.

52:18.469 --> 52:19.595
Jeez.

52:23.223 --> 52:24.933
Seriously.

52:27.519 --> 52:29.730
What am I going to do?

52:40.282 --> 52:41.950
It'll probably be fine.

52:48.874 --> 52:51.877
He seemed drunk.
He was stumbling when he walked.

52:52.628 --> 52:56.131
So you suspect he was intoxicated.

52:56.674 --> 52:59.218
Okay, we've requested
all the security footage from the area,

52:59.301 --> 53:01.553
so we'll identify the vehicle owner soon.

53:08.227 --> 53:10.729
- How may I help you?
- Well, I…

53:11.355 --> 53:12.564
Yesterday, I…

53:15.943 --> 53:16.860
ran someone over.

53:20.489 --> 53:22.658
Bong-chang just went to turn himself in.

53:24.493 --> 53:26.870
There won't be any problems for you, sir.

53:29.665 --> 53:31.041
It's not him.

53:31.125 --> 53:32.459
It wasn't this guy.

53:32.543 --> 53:33.961
I saw him.

53:35.295 --> 53:36.463
- Sir.
- Yes?

53:37.131 --> 53:39.091
Are you sure you were the one driving?

53:39.800 --> 53:43.929
Yes. I secretly took a company car out,

53:44.012 --> 53:46.598
- and made a mistake--
- You're lying.

53:46.682 --> 53:49.268
You weren't the one
who caused the accident.

53:49.351 --> 53:51.103
I saw everything!

53:51.186 --> 53:53.814
Why are you lying? Seriously!

53:53.897 --> 53:55.482
Let go of me!

53:55.566 --> 53:57.234
Sir, we have a problem.

53:57.317 --> 53:59.445
Bong-chang just called.

54:00.571 --> 54:04.199
He said he couldn't bring himself to lie
and asked if we could just forget the deal

54:04.283 --> 54:06.660
in exchange for returning
all the money we gave him.

54:06.744 --> 54:09.246
What are you talking about?
Why the sudden change?

54:09.329 --> 54:10.456
He said there was a witness.

54:14.960 --> 54:16.837
Bring that bastard here right now.

54:20.174 --> 54:22.593
- There's one more thing--
- What is it this time?

54:22.676 --> 54:24.970
I received a call from the police station.

54:25.596 --> 54:29.224
They said you also need to come in
for questioning as a witness, sir.

54:37.107 --> 54:38.776
How the hell are you…

54:40.986 --> 54:42.321
Damn it!

54:43.489 --> 54:45.032
How could you handle this so poorly?

54:46.700 --> 54:47.659
I apologize, sir.

54:54.041 --> 54:55.417
Get out.

54:56.752 --> 54:57.878
Pardon?

54:59.254 --> 55:01.089
I'll handle it myself from now on.

55:01.173 --> 55:02.257
Get out.

55:11.892 --> 55:13.227
Jeez.

55:27.491 --> 55:29.910
I WILL GRANT YOUR WISH

55:51.974 --> 55:53.058
Wow.

55:55.102 --> 55:56.311
It's you again.

56:04.361 --> 56:08.031
It must be nice to be rich,
summoning me again after just one day.

56:08.115 --> 56:10.284
Maybe I didn't charge you
enough yesterday.

56:13.245 --> 56:17.124
This time, it's a very simple job.
But it's urgent.

56:17.833 --> 56:18.834
What a shame.

56:18.917 --> 56:21.837
I was thinking of taking a break
for about ten years.

56:23.672 --> 56:26.884
An annoying old geezer
has been pestering me lately.

56:28.051 --> 56:30.387
So, I'm rejecting your request.

56:31.430 --> 56:34.474
I'll pay you double
what I gave you yesterday.

56:36.310 --> 56:38.103
I guess I'll rest
after I handle this quickly.

56:38.186 --> 56:39.104
What is it?

56:39.187 --> 56:44.484
URI GARAM HOSPITAL

57:09.509 --> 57:11.053
Who are you?

57:15.349 --> 57:16.224
You again?

57:16.308 --> 57:18.644
It seems we're deeply connected by fate.

57:20.062 --> 57:21.980
The soccer ball from yesterday, right?

57:24.066 --> 57:25.651
But how did you know I was here?

57:25.734 --> 57:26.735
Right.

57:29.071 --> 57:31.406
I'm here to tweak your memory a bit.

57:31.490 --> 57:32.616
What?

57:32.699 --> 57:35.452
Look straight at me. Don't look away.

57:41.667 --> 57:43.752
About what you saw last night…

58:07.401 --> 58:08.944
Wait a minute.

58:09.027 --> 58:10.821
This can't be happening.

58:16.660 --> 58:17.661
No way.

58:19.454 --> 58:21.707
Their fates have switched?

58:26.670 --> 58:28.338
What is this now?

58:28.422 --> 58:30.465
You're still wicked and irreverent.

58:33.260 --> 58:34.469
Your scale

58:35.012 --> 58:36.763
is tipping.

59:57.219 --> 01:00:00.138
NO TAIL TO TELL

01:00:01.056 --> 01:00:03.350
I said I lost a huge chunk
of my spiritual power.

01:00:03.433 --> 01:00:05.268
You're going to help me.

01:00:05.352 --> 01:00:07.229
I mean, what are you exactly?

01:00:07.312 --> 01:00:08.605
This beauty. And this mystique.

01:00:08.688 --> 01:00:10.482
- A demon?
- A nine-tailed fox!

01:00:10.565 --> 01:00:13.443
But no matter how much
I think about it, I just don't get it.

01:00:13.527 --> 01:00:15.070
What did I do that was so wrong?

01:00:15.153 --> 01:00:17.781
A human has died. Because of you.

01:00:19.282 --> 01:00:21.159
Kang Si-yeol.
How much does he really make?

01:00:21.243 --> 01:00:23.787
Apparently,
he makes 500 million won a week.

01:00:23.870 --> 01:00:25.831
I'm so proud that I am me.

01:00:25.914 --> 01:00:27.249
Long time no see, Si-yeol.

01:00:27.332 --> 01:00:29.376
Did he seriously not recognize me?

01:00:30.752 --> 01:00:34.089
You want to catch that hit-and-run driver
and make him pay, right?

01:00:34.631 --> 01:00:36.842
I killed someone!

01:00:36.925 --> 01:00:39.427
- Jeez!
- So, tell me. Whatever it is.

01:00:39.511 --> 01:00:40.720
What's your wish?

01:00:41.947 --> 01:00:43.947
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
